WEBVTT

01:45.522 --> 01:47.565
<i>I did it. It worked!</i>

01:48.775 --> 01:52.195
That was amazing! Absolutely amazing!

01:52.695 --> 01:53.822
Hmm.

01:53.905 --> 01:56.908
Yes, I have to admit,
I underestimated him.

01:56.991 --> 02:00.161
Those martial arts of his
are really quite something.

02:01.412 --> 02:04.791
I never thought he'd be able to
hang in there as long as he has.

02:04.874 --> 02:06.292
Huh?

02:06.376 --> 02:10.004
What in the world are you talking about?
Were you watching the same fight we were?

02:10.088 --> 02:12.882
Retsu did a whole lot more than just
"hang in there" with Pickle,

02:12.966 --> 02:14.008
he defeated him!

02:14.092 --> 02:16.344
- Hmm. Hm!
- What?

02:17.053 --> 02:19.222
Did he? I'm not so sure.

02:19.806 --> 02:22.016
Huh? Are you crazy?

02:22.100 --> 02:24.227
You saw that last crushing blow of his!

02:24.811 --> 02:27.230
<i>Good grief,
it sent Pickle back to the Stone Age!</i>

02:27.313 --> 02:29.732
<i>He suffered a bad concussion
at the very least!</i>

02:29.816 --> 02:30.900
Did he?

02:32.318 --> 02:34.654
No,
he didn't suffer any concussion.

02:35.822 --> 02:36.739
Huh?!

02:37.365 --> 02:39.617
I'm not surprised that you're surprised.

02:39.701 --> 02:42.036
You haven't been privy
to all the information.

02:43.204 --> 02:44.747
<i>After Pickle was discovered</i>

02:44.831 --> 02:48.209
<i>at the nuclear waste isolation plant
in Colorado,</i>

02:48.293 --> 02:50.503
<i>we ran a full battery of tests on him.</i>

02:51.337 --> 02:56.092
<i>His bones, organs, and muscle tissue
held many surprises for us, of course,</i>

02:56.176 --> 03:00.013
<i>but the biggest surprise of all
was his cervical spine.</i>

03:00.096 --> 03:03.516
<i>It's extraordinarily thick,
strong, and resilient,</i>

03:03.600 --> 03:07.520
<i>completely unlike the neck structure
of a typical biped, such as a human.</i>

03:07.604 --> 03:09.272
It's hard to believe,

03:09.355 --> 03:11.649
but it's only by examining
the skeletal structure

03:11.733 --> 03:14.986
of enormous four-legged beasts
with large, heavy heads

03:15.069 --> 03:18.281
that you could find a cervical spine
even remotely similar.

03:18.364 --> 03:21.284
Huh? Are you saying what I think you are?

03:21.868 --> 03:23.077
Yes.

03:23.161 --> 03:24.954
All of the anatomical evidence

03:25.038 --> 03:28.291
points to one incredible
and yet inevitable conclusion.

03:28.374 --> 03:30.835
It seems perfectly clear to me

03:30.919 --> 03:34.172
that at some point earlier
in his primeval existence,

03:34.255 --> 03:36.466
<i>Pickle was a quadruped!</i>

03:37.383 --> 03:38.384
Ha!

03:44.390 --> 03:46.351
<i>As remarkable as they may be,</i>

03:46.434 --> 03:50.813
<i>these Chinese secret arts that have
been passed down since ancient times,</i>

03:50.897 --> 03:52.523
<i>and they are indeed remarkable,</i>

03:53.024 --> 03:57.028
Those who use them have only ever targeted
others of their own kind,

03:57.111 --> 03:58.696
other human beings.

03:58.780 --> 04:01.950
Which are bipeds, not quadrupeds!

04:08.539 --> 04:09.499
Huh!

04:09.582 --> 04:13.253
<i>Can I bring the dawn of the 4,001st year?</i>

04:18.549 --> 04:19.842
<i>That stance.</i>

04:20.343 --> 04:21.803
<i>Look at that stance.</i>

04:24.055 --> 04:27.892
<i>I've never seen a forward-leaning
fight stance like that before.</i>

04:27.976 --> 04:30.478
<i>It's like the starting position
of a sprinter</i>

04:30.561 --> 04:32.647
<i>or the crouch of a sumo wrestler.</i>

04:33.398 --> 04:34.482
<i>No...</i>

04:35.400 --> 04:37.402
<i>No, it's lower to the ground than that.</i>

04:37.944 --> 04:40.488
<i>The closest thing to it
hat I can think of is...</i>

04:41.155 --> 04:41.990
<i>Yes.</i>

04:42.073 --> 04:44.742
<i>That's the attack stance of a beast.</i>

04:44.826 --> 04:46.452
<i>Just when it's about to charge,</i>

04:46.536 --> 04:48.746
<i>and every movement
other than forward propulsion</i>

04:48.830 --> 04:50.164
<i>has been abandoned.</i>

04:51.332 --> 04:55.211
<i>At this point, there's no jumping back
or dodging to the side.</i>

04:55.753 --> 04:58.423
<i>It has only one idea. To move forward.</i>

04:59.340 --> 05:01.259
<i>Then I'll answer in kind!</i>

05:01.759 --> 05:03.261
<i>I will not run.</i>

05:03.344 --> 05:05.179
<i>I will not dodge.</i>

05:05.847 --> 05:07.348
<i>I will not retreat!</i>

05:08.349 --> 05:09.976
<i>I will only attack</i>

05:10.852 --> 05:13.604
<i>with this weapon that symbolizes kung fu,</i>

05:13.688 --> 05:15.064
<i>the Crushing Fist!</i>

05:15.606 --> 05:17.108
<i>I will attack him head-on,</i>

05:17.608 --> 05:20.361
<i>and punch a hole right through him!</i>

05:20.862 --> 05:23.406
<i>And at that moment,
the beast erupted.</i>

05:23.906 --> 05:26.451
<i>It was as if
his whole body turned to flame.</i>

05:28.286 --> 05:31.247
<i>It was just like
when he vanquished the T. rex,</i>

05:31.331 --> 05:33.499
<i>or smashed the mighty triceratops,</i>

05:33.583 --> 05:36.252
<i>or chased away the towering brachiosaurus...</i>

05:37.128 --> 05:40.673
<i>This attack he used only
against his strongest enemies,</i>

05:40.757 --> 05:42.592
<i>the greatest of his day,</i>

05:42.675 --> 05:46.512
<i>he now unleashed upon
that extraordinary kung fu fighter,</i>

05:46.596 --> 05:48.681
<i>Sea King Retsu!</i>

05:53.519 --> 05:57.023
<i>In a contest between
an immoveable modern-day shield</i>

05:57.106 --> 05:59.359
<i>and an irresistible ancient spear,</i>

05:59.442 --> 06:03.321
<i>on this day at least,
the spear was the winner.</i>

06:07.158 --> 06:09.952
He's just too powerful.

06:10.620 --> 06:14.040
He never even got a chance
to use his big move on him.

06:14.123 --> 06:14.957
Huh?

06:20.797 --> 06:22.465
He's... crying again!

06:30.181 --> 06:31.140
He's not?

06:31.224 --> 06:35.436
Don't look so surprised, Tokugawa.
It's the most natural thing in the world.

06:35.520 --> 06:38.356
What does any animal do
when it's worked up an appetite?

06:39.690 --> 06:42.110
It sits down to a good meal.

06:42.193 --> 06:44.112
Huh? Professor.

06:44.195 --> 06:46.864
We're not...
we're not really going to let him--

06:46.948 --> 06:47.907
Hmm...

06:50.076 --> 06:53.037
Tokugawa,
we made a bargain with Pickle.

06:53.121 --> 06:55.832
Would you have us break
our side of the bargain?

06:55.915 --> 06:56.874
Argh!

06:56.958 --> 06:59.710
You're not saying
you'd let Pickle eat him?!

06:59.794 --> 07:01.379
Don't drag me into it.

07:01.462 --> 07:03.381
<i>I'm</i> not the one
who thought it was a good idea

07:03.464 --> 07:04.882
sending Retsu in there with him.

07:04.966 --> 07:08.553
Oh, it's my fault?!
Don't you try blaming me for this!

07:08.636 --> 07:11.889
Wait, wait, wait! Pickle, wait!
That wasn't part of the bargain!

07:13.975 --> 07:15.393
Pickle! Stop!

07:15.977 --> 07:17.270
Don't do it.

07:17.812 --> 07:19.897
That man is a fierce and noble warrior!

07:19.981 --> 07:22.859
A proud fighter who thought
of nothing else, day or night,

07:22.942 --> 07:24.402
but of meeting you in combat!

07:24.485 --> 07:27.155
He deserves to be your comrade,
not your dinner!

07:27.738 --> 07:29.907
Damn it, man, where's your humanity?

07:50.261 --> 07:53.139
<i>Eating can be
a way of saying farewell,</i>

07:53.681 --> 07:55.558
<i>but it is a damnable fate.</i>

07:57.351 --> 07:59.562
<i>His appetite was ferocious.</i>

08:00.438 --> 08:05.443
<i>Still, the primitive man's heart
was filled with sorrow.</i>

08:05.526 --> 08:06.569
Huh?

08:10.990 --> 08:12.450
<i>Food and life.</i>

08:13.409 --> 08:14.827
<i>Life and death.</i>

08:15.661 --> 08:17.830
<i>The two cannot be separated.</i>

08:20.708 --> 08:23.336
<i>The two cannot be separated.</i>

08:46.901 --> 08:48.861
<i>I'm ashamed of myself!</i>

08:48.945 --> 08:51.113
<i>I broke my pledge to Pickle!</i>

08:52.281 --> 08:53.991
<i>I as good as lied to him.</i>

08:54.575 --> 08:56.619
<i>"If I lost, I would be eaten."</i>

08:57.537 --> 08:59.497
<i>Isn't that the pledge I made?</i>

09:00.581 --> 09:02.625
<i>Then why am I still here?</i>

09:03.417 --> 09:08.089
<i>All I sacrificed was a piece
of my shoulder and a part of my leg.</i>

09:08.714 --> 09:09.966
<i>That's not enough.</i>

09:10.967 --> 09:14.178
<i>Was I ever really serious
about fulfilling my pledge</i>

09:14.804 --> 09:16.556
<i>and letting him eat me?</i>

09:17.473 --> 09:18.724
<i>Perhaps not.</i>

09:19.559 --> 09:23.312
<i>Perhaps deep in my heart,
I feared being eaten.</i>

09:23.980 --> 09:25.565
<i>I wanted to survive.</i>

09:26.315 --> 09:27.858
<i>That's it, isn't it?</i>

09:28.484 --> 09:30.444
<i>Oh, the dishonor of it!</i>

09:33.406 --> 09:34.782
So it is true.

09:37.868 --> 09:39.453
You were bitten.

09:40.329 --> 09:41.872
Or rather, you were eaten.

09:42.748 --> 09:45.710
When they told me what that caveman did,

09:46.460 --> 09:47.628
I didn't believe 'em.

09:55.595 --> 09:56.804
So, how you holding up?

09:57.388 --> 09:58.222
You okay?

09:58.306 --> 09:59.932
Hm! Never better.

10:02.727 --> 10:03.811
Really?

10:04.895 --> 10:07.106
Well, am I less than ecstatic about it?

10:07.607 --> 10:08.649
Yes, I am.

10:09.442 --> 10:10.818
Am I a little upset?

10:11.402 --> 10:13.154
I'd be lying to say I'm not.

10:13.237 --> 10:14.071
Okay.

10:14.155 --> 10:16.157
I'm a fighter who lost a fight.

10:16.824 --> 10:18.576
And part of my body as well.

10:19.243 --> 10:21.078
But there is no dishonor in that.

10:21.162 --> 10:22.747
Definitely not.

10:22.830 --> 10:24.874
No, my shame lies elsewhere.

10:26.375 --> 10:28.711
I boasted of a courage I didn't have.

10:29.503 --> 10:32.381
I claimed that I was ready
to face the consequences,

10:32.465 --> 10:33.341
when I wasn't.

10:33.424 --> 10:35.343
That's not what Tokugawa said.

10:35.885 --> 10:37.178
He told me all about it.

10:38.179 --> 10:41.182
From everything I heard,
you have nothing to be ashamed of.

10:41.265 --> 10:42.099
Don't I?

10:42.600 --> 10:45.269
Neither you nor he
can know for sure, can you?

10:46.437 --> 10:47.938
At the end of the day,

10:48.022 --> 10:50.858
the only person who really knows
the answer to that is me.

10:53.194 --> 10:54.820
"To give one's all."

10:55.404 --> 10:56.947
To be "prepared to die"

10:57.531 --> 10:58.824
or "ready to kill."

11:00.242 --> 11:01.994
People say the words,

11:02.078 --> 11:03.871
but do they ever really mean them?

11:04.955 --> 11:06.499
They're just empty words

11:07.041 --> 11:09.001
without the willpower to back them up.

11:09.543 --> 11:10.920
I'd been forewarned.

11:11.504 --> 11:13.214
I accepted the consequences.

11:14.548 --> 11:16.509
And yet, I broke my pledge.

11:17.093 --> 11:18.636
Tokugawa.

11:19.428 --> 11:21.764
What if you were to feed me to Pickle?

11:22.807 --> 11:24.809
I offered myself before

11:24.892 --> 11:26.477
I knew what the words meant.

11:29.355 --> 11:30.856
That is my dishonor.

11:34.068 --> 11:36.529
You made yourself a perfect fighter.

11:36.612 --> 11:39.031
Turned your body into a living weapon.

11:39.115 --> 11:40.658
That's been taken from you.

11:41.784 --> 11:42.910
And that's gotta hurt.

11:44.995 --> 11:48.165
But it's not your missing leg
that's causing you pain.

11:48.916 --> 11:50.376
You're hurting inside.

11:50.960 --> 11:54.213
But I'm telling you,
you should take pride in that pain.

11:56.006 --> 11:59.093
Sea King Retsu is
a legendary martial artist.

11:59.593 --> 12:02.847
You're a living national treasure
of the People's Republic of China.

12:04.557 --> 12:05.933
Hmph.

12:06.600 --> 12:08.811
You know your name has
a really cool meaning.

12:10.146 --> 12:11.939
I looked it up a while ago.

12:13.566 --> 12:14.483
<i>Retsu.</i>

12:14.984 --> 12:16.068
<i>It means fierce,</i>

12:16.861 --> 12:19.822
<i>intense, never straying from the path,</i>

12:21.532 --> 12:23.451
always laser focused.

12:23.534 --> 12:25.536
That's exactly who you are.

12:26.579 --> 12:29.039
Your fighting skills are
so insanely impressive

12:29.123 --> 12:31.417
that that's all people ever think about.

12:32.042 --> 12:36.589
But your real worth lies
in the strength of your incredible spirit.

12:38.966 --> 12:40.217
Thank you, Baki.

12:46.932 --> 12:48.017
Means a lot.

12:53.355 --> 12:55.649
<i>I remember sometimes hearing my dad</i>

12:55.733 --> 12:58.194
<i>talkin' about a fight
and saying that he was gonna</i>

12:59.153 --> 13:00.821
<i>“eat the guy alive.”</i>

13:00.905 --> 13:03.407
<i>But it was just a metaphor.</i>

13:04.200 --> 13:06.911
<i>It meant he was gonna beat him.
He was gonna win.</i>

13:06.994 --> 13:10.122
<i>But with this guy,
it's not just a figure of speech...</i>

13:11.290 --> 13:13.125
<i>He really does eat 'em alive.</i>

13:13.793 --> 13:15.836
Heh. I'm tellin' ya,

13:16.879 --> 13:19.048
this caveman is really something else.

13:20.216 --> 13:22.134
KASHIMA DAIMYOJIN
KATORI DAIMYOJIN

13:46.242 --> 13:49.036
<i>This must be
the famous needle-cut move.</i>

14:02.675 --> 14:03.676
Whoa.

14:03.759 --> 14:06.220
Cleaner than a Japanese blade
could've done it.

14:06.303 --> 14:07.680
- Sir!
- Huh?

14:07.763 --> 14:09.557
Excuse me. Call for you.

14:10.057 --> 14:11.183
Right.

14:12.351 --> 14:16.188
Noble Elder, please calm down.
I'm having a hard time following you.

14:16.897 --> 14:20.693
It sounded like you said
that Sea King Retsu has been eaten.

14:21.861 --> 14:22.695
Pickle?

14:23.279 --> 14:25.573
You're saying Retsu got beaten by Pickle?

14:25.656 --> 14:28.117
<i>I didn't say that!
It's not that simple !</i>

14:28.617 --> 14:31.370
- It isn't?
<i>- It's not that he was beaten really.</i>

14:31.453 --> 14:34.206
<i>- But he was... he was--</i>
- So, you are saying he was eaten?

14:35.124 --> 14:38.210
- But he didn't lose. Really?
-<i>Yes, exactly!</i>

14:38.294 --> 14:39.295
DOPPO

14:39.378 --> 14:42.006
So, the two of them fought,
and then...

14:42.840 --> 14:44.884
Oh, I see.

14:44.967 --> 14:47.052
His shoulder and his leg, huh?

14:47.761 --> 14:49.972
Got it. All right.

14:54.435 --> 14:55.561
Hmm.

14:58.105 --> 14:58.939
Sir?

14:59.440 --> 15:01.275
- We need to talk.
- 'Course.

15:02.943 --> 15:04.361
You're joking, sir.

15:04.987 --> 15:07.364
How could Sea King Retsu
have been defeated?

15:07.448 --> 15:09.950
This isn't about whether he won or lost.

15:10.034 --> 15:11.619
That's not what's important.

15:12.202 --> 15:13.954
It's about what came after,

15:14.038 --> 15:18.125
when that great fighter
was reduced to food and eaten.

15:22.212 --> 15:23.964
That disrespectful little--

15:24.048 --> 15:25.257
Who do you mean?

15:26.675 --> 15:30.137
Who d'you think I mean?!
The damn Jurassic monkey, of course!

15:33.182 --> 15:35.351
Katsumi, you just don't get it, do you?

15:35.434 --> 15:37.186
You think he's underestimating us?

15:38.228 --> 15:40.898
You couldn't be more wrong.
Trust me on this.

15:43.484 --> 15:46.070
No. We don't matter enough to him.

15:46.153 --> 15:49.156
He doesn't even deem us worthy
of being underestimated.

15:49.239 --> 15:51.825
Isn't that exactly
what underestimating is?

15:51.909 --> 15:53.410
Katsumi!

15:53.494 --> 15:55.996
Before someone can underestimate you,

15:56.497 --> 15:59.416
they have to at least recognize
that you even exist.

16:00.084 --> 16:01.919
We're just a meal to Pickle.

16:02.002 --> 16:06.423
Do you and I "underestimate"
the meat and fish we eat for dinner?

16:09.510 --> 16:12.179
Sir, I think maybe
you're the one who doesn't get it.

16:12.930 --> 16:14.682
The way you think about it,

16:14.765 --> 16:17.935
not underestimating us
is the same as underestimating us!

16:18.018 --> 16:19.144
Huh?

16:21.563 --> 16:22.940
Well, Katsumi.

16:23.774 --> 16:25.693
You may have a point.

16:25.776 --> 16:27.653
SHINSHINKAI HEADQUARTERS A WAY OF KARATE

16:27.736 --> 16:30.572
<i>Sea King Retsu had been eaten.</i>

16:31.407 --> 16:36.704
<i>The startling news spread like wildfire
through the Atsugi Base reunion members.</i>

16:46.296 --> 16:47.798
That should've been enough anesthetic

16:47.881 --> 16:50.718
to knock out a bull elephant
for a full day!

16:50.801 --> 16:52.678
That was just a couple of hours ago!

16:53.303 --> 16:57.224
It certainly isn't the sort of thing
you see every day, that's for sure.

16:57.307 --> 17:01.478
In fact, there was only one other time
that someone broke through that door.

17:05.315 --> 17:07.735
<i>And you know who that was.</i>

17:07.818 --> 17:09.486
<i>Yujiro Hanma.</i>

17:16.076 --> 17:18.746
<i>Takeshi Kenmochi, age 21.</i>

17:19.663 --> 17:21.749
<i>He was a big, strong-looking young man.</i>

17:22.499 --> 17:24.418
<i>And indeed, he was strong.</i>

17:25.210 --> 17:26.462
<i>Very strong.</i>

17:27.129 --> 17:28.005
<i>Karate.</i>

17:28.088 --> 17:29.256
<i>Boxing.</i>

17:29.840 --> 17:31.133
<i>Weightlifting.</i>

17:31.842 --> 17:34.511
<i>In all the many dojos
and gyms he frequented,</i>

17:34.595 --> 17:36.764
<i>there was no one who could match him.</i>

17:38.140 --> 17:41.977
<i>So what was this Kenmochi doing here,
amid all this nightlife?</i>

17:42.853 --> 17:45.022
<i>He was looking for someone to fight.</i>

17:47.357 --> 17:48.484
<i>He wouldn't kill them,</i>

17:48.984 --> 17:51.236
<i>but he wouldn't
leave them uninjured either.</i>

17:51.779 --> 17:55.282
<i>He was on the prowl,
searching for the perfect someone.</i>

18:52.172 --> 18:55.425
<i>Color. Color. Light.</i>

18:56.009 --> 18:58.095
<i>Color. Fire?</i>

18:58.679 --> 19:00.556
<i>Stars? Heat?</i>

19:01.682 --> 19:04.101
<i>Crowds. Crowds.</i>

19:04.184 --> 19:05.102
<i>Food.</i>

19:06.687 --> 19:08.188
<i>Straight lines.</i>

19:08.272 --> 19:09.189
<i>Vertical.</i>

19:09.690 --> 19:10.983
<i>Straight lines.</i>

19:11.692 --> 19:12.526
<i>Horizontal.</i>

19:13.026 --> 19:14.111
<i>Sky.</i>

19:14.194 --> 19:15.487
<i>Ground.</i>

19:15.988 --> 19:17.114
<i>Flat ground.</i>

19:17.948 --> 19:19.324
<i>Straight lines.</i>

19:19.408 --> 19:21.326
<i>He was confused.</i>

19:21.410 --> 19:23.162
<i>Nothing here was familiar to him.</i>

19:23.704 --> 19:25.539
<i>He had never felt more lost.</i>

19:27.958 --> 19:29.126
<i>In his own era,</i>

19:29.209 --> 19:31.712
<i>he ate only those things
that attacked him.</i>

19:31.795 --> 19:32.629
<i>Fight.</i>

19:32.713 --> 19:33.881
<i>Win.</i>

19:33.964 --> 19:34.798
<i>Eat.</i>

19:36.216 --> 19:37.718
<i>He had been proud then.</i>

19:38.260 --> 19:39.511
<i>What is he now?</i>

19:40.262 --> 19:43.223
<i>Now he wears these clothes as a disguise.</i>

19:43.891 --> 19:46.393
<i>He must wear them
in order to survive here.</i>

19:47.728 --> 19:49.605
<i>He understands that much.</i>

19:51.857 --> 19:53.942
<i>He's six and a half feet tall</i>

19:54.026 --> 19:57.404
<i>and weighs more than 285 pounds.</i>

